sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-12> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-12--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-12--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch15-12: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.74" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.736"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Both halves of the claim are numerical, so a large human sample can confirm or reject the factor of six to seven. Open MRI supplies the thickness ratio directly, and published catheterization series supply the pressure ratio for the same species. Other mammals are less uniformly measured, but a systematic departure in humans would already refute the proportion as a general mammalian fact." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Estimate mean left-ventricular and right-ventricular wall thickness in the same hearts and compare their ratio with the ratio of systolic cavity pressures. The claim is confirmed if both ratios fall near 6-7 and match each other; a thickness ratio far from the pressure ratio, or either ratio far from 6-7, refutes it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Ventricular pressure ratios are widely tabulated in clinical series and are weakly paired with the same open imaging files.", "Where along the wall the thickness is taken changes the ratio." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-12--grok--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-12--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch15-12 by Grok 4.7: 0.9" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.9"^^xsd:double ;
